            0.884,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You may have seen rocks in your surroundings. Rocks are used in the construction of houses, buildings, temples, roads, dams and table tops. Some rocks, like slate, are used for roofing (Fig. 11.6) and laterite can be used as a building material, like bricks (Fig. 11.7). Some of the important rocks are granite, sandstone and marble. Human beings have been using rocks to make tools such as hand axes (Fig. 11.8a) and arrowheads (Fig. 11.8b) since thousands of years."
            }
          ]
        },
